    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Bryson Stott** (70.27) anchor the lineup as our strongest offensive weapons. **Taylor Ward** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Erick Fedde, whose 5.20 xERA is the most exploitable mark on the board; when combined with a park factor boost of 16% and a favorable wind-out condition, he is a primary start. Similarly, **Bryson Stott** draws a matchup against Bubba Chandler that is bolstered by a 13% dynamic platoon edge, making him a high-efficiency play for both counting stats and batting average stability. **Tyler Freeman** (69.11) also demands attention; while the matchup against Eury P\u00e9rez is tougher, **Tyler Freeman** possesses an underrated \"stolen base\" narrative here, as the slow delivery of the opposition combined with his own sprint profile creates a high-ceiling scenario for the scarcest category in our 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins involved **Jung Hoo Lee**, whose 48.58 score narrowly missed the cutoff. While **Jung Hoo Lee** provides a reliable floor, the optimizer prioritized the specific platoon advantages of **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and the high-leverage order spot of **Matt Chapman** (58.92). **Matt Chapman** serves as a vital cog in the lineup today, and we are proceeding with caution regarding **Cal Raleigh** (52.46) and **Yainer Diaz** (40.19); both are currently subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status, and **Yainer Diaz** faces a daunting 3.21 xERA from Joe Ryan, necessitating a lower confidence start. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while keeping **Gavin Sheets** and **Drew Gilbert** on the bench as high-variance contingency options should any late-scratches occur. Ensure all lineups are locked before first pitch, as the reliance on estimated batting orders adds a layer of risk to our daily efficiency targets.",
